            "Python ctypes, c_int32: https://docs.python.org/3/library/ctypes.html#fundamental-data-types"
          ],
          "conclusion": "Python int arithmetic has unlimited precision, so ordinary scalar integer addition does not have signed 32-bit overflow semantics. ctypes.c_int32 provides 32-bit storage/conversion but arithmetic on exposed Python values is Python integer arithmetic followed by conversion, which is a storage/conversion substitute rather than the canonical signed-32-bit scalar operation.",
